Arch Linux
sudo pacman -Syu

Install QEMU, KVM, libvirt, virt-manager and related tools
sudo pacman -S qemu-full libvirt virt-manager virt-install virt-viewer dnsmasq bridge-utils edk2-ovmf

Enable and start the libvirt service
sudo systemctl enable --now libvirtd

Add your user to the libvirt group
sudo usermod -aG libvirt $(whoami)

(Optional) Add your user to the kvm group
sudo usermod -aG kvm $(whoami)

Verify virtualization support
sudo virt-host-validate

Launch Virtual Machine Manager
virt-manager

share folder in qemu to host

qemu-system-x86_64 \
  -enable-kvm \
  -m 4G \
  -smp 4 \
  -drive arch.qcow2 \
  -fsdev local,id=shared_folder_id,path=/path/to/host/folder,security_model=mapped-xattr \
  -device virtio-9p-pci,fsdev=shared_folder_id,mount_tag=host_share




path=/path/to/host/folder: 
The absolute path to the folder on your host machine that you want to 
share.id=shared_folder_id: An internal identifier QEMU uses to connect the device
to the backend file system 
storage.mount_tag=host_share: 
The text "label" the guest system will look for when mounting the folder. 
You can name this whatever you like.security_model=mapped-xattr: 
Ensures file permissions (UID/GID) are preserved properly between host and guest.

